\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Confirmatory and scaling results across fresh seeds, longer horizon, and greater width.} Held-out reports final cross-entropy $\mathcal  {L}_{\mathrm  {sel}}$ in nats; all $\Delta $ columns report differences from same-regime Muon in millinats (negative favors the row method). MuonT applies input preconditioning only, so the gap between the MuonT and Muon2-ExpDiag rows isolates the output-side contribution. Late-11 averages the 11 second-half checkpoints; Wins counts the 16 Paloma domains improved over Muon. All four methods share their verified seed-0 optimum within each regime ($\eta ^*=0.01600$ at 130M and 520M 20 TPP, and $0.01600\times 4^{-0.3}=0.01056$ at 130M 80 TPP). Complete absolute losses and $\eta =0.02263$ replicates appear in \Cref  {tab:absolute_results,tab:seeds}.}}{13}{table.caption.27}\protected@file@percent }
