\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Frobenius Hyperball retraction across Muon, MuonHT, and Muon2-ExpDiagH at 130M (20 TPP, 2.68B tokens).} Following \Cref  {tab:main_scaling}, Held-out reports final cross-entropy $\mathcal  {L}_{\mathrm  {sel}}$ in nats and all $\Delta $ columns report differences from same-seed Muon ($\eta ^*=0.01600$) in millinats (negative favors the row method). Replacing decoupled weight decay with Frobenius Hyperball retraction~\citep  {wen2026hyperball} fixes $\|W_t\|_F=\|W_0\|_F$ and normalizes $D_t/\|D_t\|_F$, shifting the shared full-budget interior optimum down by one $\sqrt  {2}$ grid step from $\eta ^*=0.01600$ to $\eta ^*_{\mathrm  {HB}}=0.01131$ across all three Hyperball variants (MuonH, input-preconditioned MuonHT, and structure-aware two-sided Muon2-ExpDiagH). Entries marked --- await completion of the final multi-seed and 16-domain Paloma evaluations.}}{21}{table.caption.48}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{brf}{\backcite{wen2026hyperball}{{21}{8}{table.caption.48}}}
